#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:50004
#: 8f519d3d81d24a17acfc85126920eedf
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Let's consider a simple example where we have a downstream business "
"outcome (new users) and a set of upper-funnel channels (`impressions_x1`,"
" `impressions_x2`, `impressions_x3`, `impressions_x4`) (this synthetic "
"data is generated in the advanced version of this notebook "
"{ref}`mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach`)."
msgstr ""
"Consideremos un ejemplo sencillo en el que tenemos un resultado de negocio "
"posterior (nuevos usuarios) y un conjunto de canales de la parte superior "
"del embudo (`impressions_x1`, `impressions_x2`, `impressions_x3`, "
"`impressions_x4`) (estos datos sintéticos se generan en la versión avanzada "
"de este cuaderno {ref}`mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach`)."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:70002
#: 7f2a66005b3e49908f487bf8d9369f1a
msgid "Let's look at the data:"
msgstr "Veamos los datos:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:90002
#: 8ffb26402e334a8cb623e20cf1e93c9f
msgid "We have a `target_var` that we want to predict."
msgstr "Tenemos una variable `target_var` que queremos predecir."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:90003
#: fac4f89831554e80818aa609db89f4c3
msgid ""
"We have 4 upper-funnel channels: `impressions_x1`, `impressions_x2`, "
"`impressions_x3`, `impressions_x4`."
msgstr ""
"Tenemos 4 canales de la parte superior del embudo: `impressions_x1`, "
"`impressions_x2`, `impressions_x3`, `impressions_x4`."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:90004
#: d1a0c797b9e6433bbacfdd50ccdb721f
msgid ""
"We have some control variables: `holidays`, `trend`, `event_2020_09`, "
"`event_2020_12`, `event_2021_09`, `event_2021_12`, `event_2022_09` "
"(events look like Gaussian bumps)."
msgstr ""
"Tenemos algunas variables de control: `holidays`, `trend`, `event_2020_09`, "
"`event_2020_12`, `event_2021_09`, `event_2021_12`, `event_2022_09` (los "
"eventos parecen picos gaussianos)."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:100002
#: 7c3ba2d593f54a918eb17444f961bb00
msgid "Let us visualize the impressions data in detail:"
msgstr "Visualicemos en detalle los datos de impresiones:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:120002
#: 995f101bede94ee0bde42e41ff4a653b
msgid "Causal DAG"
msgstr "DAG causal"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:120004
#: 098dc5b915b6486389f03b1065fde072
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"As described in the introduction, understanding the causal structure of "
"the marketing funnel is key to correctly attribute the effect of each "
"channel. A simple, put-all-channels-in-one-model approach will lead to "
"biased estimates (see {ref}`mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach` for a "
"comparison)."
msgstr ""
"Como se describió en la introducción, comprender la estructura causal del "
"embudo de marketing es clave para atribuir correctamente el efecto de cada "
"canal. Un enfoque simple de poner todos los canales en un solo modelo "
"conducirá a estimaciones sesgadas (véase "
"{ref}`mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach` para una comparación)."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:120006
#: 644f42f4ada74d9f90a221cb812364b3
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"A common and handy structure to encode causal relationships is the causal"
" directed acyclic graph (DAG). Each node represents a variable, and each "
"arrow represents a causal relationship. This DAG does not come from the "
"data, but rather from our understanding of the marketing funnel for the "
"concrete application (one can use causal discovery methods to learn some "
"structure of the DAG from the data, but that is out of scope for this "
"notebook, see {ref}`mmm_causal_reasoning_and_discovery`)."
msgstr ""
"Una estructura común y práctica para codificar relaciones causales es el "
"grafo acíclico dirigido (DAG) causal. Cada nodo representa una variable y "
"cada flecha representa una relación causal. Este DAG no proviene de los "
"datos, sino de nuestra comprensión del embudo de marketing para la "
"aplicación concreta (se pueden usar métodos de descubrimiento causal para "
"aprender parte de la estructura del DAG a partir de los datos, pero eso "
"queda fuera del alcance de este cuaderno, véase "
"{ref}`mmm_causal_reasoning_and_discovery`)."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:120008
#: 75ae2dd3636c41918681f8bfe6b73c73
msgid ""
"The DAG below shows our hypothesis about the structure of our marketing "
"funnel. This diagram represents our understanding of how marketing "
"channels influence each other and ultimately drive the outcome."
msgstr ""
"El DAG a continuación muestra nuestra hipótesis sobre la estructura de "
"nuestro embudo de marketing. Este diagrama representa nuestra comprensión de"
" cómo los canales de marketing se influyen entre sí y, en última instancia, "
"impulsan el resultado."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:120010
#: 36e1322501984fed9b377f1ee6d4a375
msgid "**Key components:**"
msgstr "**Componentes clave:**"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:120012
#: ffa4b25dd3a54affbd27f51027736b22
msgid ""
"**X1 (impressions_x1)**: Upper-funnel awareness channel (e.g., video, "
"display ads)"
msgstr ""
"**X1 (impressions_x1)**: canal de notoriedad de la parte superior del embudo"
" (por ejemplo, video, anuncios display)"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:120013
#: f309c242c2074e6c9073be726d6f9900
msgid ""
"**X2, X3 (impressions_x2, impressions_x3)**: Mid-funnel consideration "
"channels (social engagement, remarketing)"
msgstr ""
"**X2, X3 (impressions_x2, impressions_x3)**: canales de consideración de la "
"parte media del embudo (interacción en redes sociales, remarketing)"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:120014
#: 6f747adad0ad43efbfab65591a4712f1
msgid "**X4 (impressions_x4)**: Lower-funnel high-intent channel (brand search)"
msgstr ""
"**X4 (impressions_x4)**: canal de alta intención de la parte inferior del "
"embudo (búsqueda de marca)"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:120015
#: 5df559b15a884ea09d29a91c0906733e
msgid "**Y (new users)**: Business outcome"
msgstr "**Y (nuevos usuarios)**: resultado de negocio"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:120016
#: a96947db87ba429cabf147bdcfc7c2f9
msgid "**U1, U2, U3, U4**: Exogenous factors affecting each channel (unobserved)"
msgstr ""
"**U1, U2, U3, U4**: factores exógenos que afectan a cada canal (no "
"observados)"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:120018
#: 595ad429ca414ec8a4a8c5593dcb8b40
msgid "**The funnel structure:**"
msgstr "**La estructura del embudo:**"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:120020
#: 6111f984d2e04cc4a456d9c396e68166
msgid "X_1 \\to (X_2, X_3) \\to X_4 \\to Y"
msgstr "X_1 \\to (X_2, X_3) \\to X_4 \\to Y"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:120022
#: f672294d4fda487f888dc8d54f0e7903
msgid ""
"Notice that **X1 does not directly affect Y**. Its influence flows "
"entirely through the downstream channels. This mediation structure is "
"critical: if we model all channels as directly affecting Y (the \"throw "
"everything in\" approach), we'll misattribute effects and either over- or"
" under-credit upper-funnel investments."
msgstr ""
"Observe que **X1 no afecta directamente a Y**. Su influencia fluye por "
"completo a través de los canales posteriores. Esta estructura de mediación "
"es crítica: si modelamos todos los canales como si afectaran directamente a "
"Y (el enfoque de \"meter todo\"), atribuiremos mal los efectos y "
"sobreestimaremos o subestimaremos las inversiones de la parte superior del "
"embudo."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:120024
#: 3f7a64f10a2249b492f5aba696bf4ac6
msgid ""
"The dashed nodes represent unobserved factors (holidays, budget changes, "
"competitor actions) that can shift channels independently."
msgstr ""
"Los nodos de línea discontinua representan factores no observados (feriados,"
" cambios de presupuesto, acciones de la competencia) que pueden modificar "
"los canales de forma independiente."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:140002
#: 9fc69b4bc4ff455e80245f702d603822
msgid ""
"To measure the indirect effect of X1 (upper funnel) on Y (outcome), we "
"use a **two-model approach**:"
msgstr ""
"Para medir el efecto indirecto de X1 (parte superior del embudo) sobre Y "
"(resultado), usamos un **enfoque de dos modelos**:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:140004
#: e28a0f85e8e24f21b8abf0281e60f8aa
msgid ""
"**Direct Model (Outcome Model)**: Estimates how X4 (lower funnel) affects"
" Y"
msgstr ""
"**Modelo directo (modelo del resultado)**: estima cómo X4 (parte inferior "
"del embudo) afecta a Y"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:140005
#: 76c49d44fecf44549834f2d62a98a8d8
msgid "Includes adstock (carryover effects) and saturation (diminishing returns)"
msgstr ""
"Incluye adstock (efectos de arrastre) y saturación (rendimientos "
"decrecientes)"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:140006
#: 85cbfdaad34a42fd9a2f3c16d75dc2ac
msgid "Only models the final step: $X_4 \\to Y$"
msgstr "Solo modela el paso final: $X_4 \\to Y$"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:140008
#: f1ac1a90304c4b6ab37b70d43412a970
msgid ""
"**Indirect Model (Mediation Model)**: Estimates how X1 (upper funnel) "
"affects X4 (lower funnel)"
msgstr ""
"**Modelo indirecto (modelo de mediación)**: estima cómo X1 (parte superior "
"del embudo) afecta a X4 (parte inferior del embudo)"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:140009
#: 9049d1df31524539910075e8addc47e0
msgid "Captures the propagation through the funnel: $X_1 \\to X_4$"
msgstr "Captura la propagación a través del embudo: $X_1 \\to X_4$"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:140010
#: 073aef9a1a614e41a295b1e7389688c6
msgid "Uses simpler transformations since this link is more direct"
msgstr "Usa transformaciones más simples, ya que este vínculo es más directo"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:140012
#: b5a84207205249fd80df4ff75adf2fb5
msgid "By separating these two relationships, we can:"
msgstr "Al separar estas dos relaciones, podemos:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:140013
#: 9a20479c400a4deaa4bc0062353da9a3
msgid "Respect the causal structure from our DAG"
msgstr "Respetar la estructura causal de nuestro DAG"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:140014
#: 59afc00be9724acfbd1e4e5279295b12
msgid "Avoid confounding the indirect path with the direct effect"
msgstr "Evitar confundir la ruta indirecta con el efecto directo"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:140015
#: 0be6acc2818442819bfc702fb6c77803
msgid "Generate counterfactuals to ask \"what if X1 had been zero?\""
msgstr ""
"Generar contrafactuales para preguntar \"¿qué habría pasado si X1 hubiera "
"sido cero?\""

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:140017
#: 23cba41ea0cb4cd7ac705b41d8aa8d05
msgid ""
"**Why not just include all channels in one model?** Because that approach"
" ignores mediation. It would try to estimate a direct $X_1 \\to Y$ effect"
" (which doesn't exist in our causal story) and would misattribute the "
"propagated effect through $X_4$."
msgstr ""
"**¿Por qué no simplemente incluir todos los canales en un solo modelo?** "
"Porque ese enfoque ignora la mediación. Intentaría estimar un efecto directo"
" $X_1 \\to Y$ (que no existe en nuestra historia causal) y atribuiría mal el"
" efecto propagado a través de $X_4$."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:150002
#: c757e159690f4712a85c074eff267dc8
msgid "Data Preparation"
msgstr "Preparación de los datos"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:150004
#: a4886e5219364a5795e08c98ffda58d5
msgid ""
"We split the data into training and test sets to evaluate how well our "
"causal model generalizes. The training set will be used to fit both our "
"outcome model and our mediation model."
msgstr ""
"Dividimos los datos en conjuntos de entrenamiento y de prueba para evaluar "
"qué tan bien generaliza nuestro modelo causal. El conjunto de entrenamiento "
"se usará para ajustar tanto nuestro modelo del resultado como nuestro modelo"
" de mediación."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:170002
#: de3cce77f5f541519263dc55c81de0a8
msgid ""
"**Control columns** include trend and event indicators. These represent "
"factors that affect the outcome but are not marketing channels (holidays,"
" seasonality, special events). Including them ensures we don't "
"misattribute their effects to our channels."
msgstr ""
"**Las columnas de control** incluyen la tendencia y los indicadores de "
"eventos. Estas representan factores que afectan al resultado pero que no son"
" canales de marketing (feriados, estacionalidad, eventos especiales). "
"Incluirlas garantiza que no atribuyamos erróneamente sus efectos a nuestros "
"canales."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:190002
#: 241357589772462baccbe09d3dc9681d
msgid "Model Specification"
msgstr "Especificación del modelo"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:190004
#: 33d2a2c48cae4c7fafcdb8196b7ce9ee
msgid "Now we are ready to specify both models in PyMC-Marketing."
msgstr ""
"Ahora estamos listos para especificar ambos modelos en PyMC-Marketing."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:200002
#: a4335dde31ec434cb5ee361437d48b4c
msgid "Direct Model"
msgstr "Modelo directo"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:210002
#: adbb2f0db2b64953989d402554ace8db
msgid ""
"The first model captures how the **lower-funnel channel (X4) drives the "
"outcome (Y)**. This is the most direct relationship in our funnel and "
"includes the dynamic effects we expect in marketing:"
msgstr ""
"El primer modelo captura cómo el **canal de la parte inferior del embudo "
"(X4) impulsa el resultado (Y)**. Esta es la relación más directa de nuestro "
"embudo e incluye los efectos dinámicos que esperamos en marketing:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:210004
#: d405ad3005754bd1be412f86d2226a23
msgid ""
"**Adstock (Geometric)**: Marketing effects don't disappear immediately. "
"Today's exposure influences tomorrow's outcome with some decay rate "
"$\\alpha$. The `l_max=24` parameter means we allow up to $24$ days of "
"carryover."
msgstr ""
"**Adstock (geométrico)**: los efectos del marketing no desaparecen de "
"inmediato. La exposición de hoy influye en el resultado de mañana con cierta"
" tasa de decaimiento $\\alpha$. El parámetro `l_max=24` significa que "
"permitimos hasta $24$ días de efecto de arrastre."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:210006
#: d9e89071a8544b4db47a77b739ccf552
msgid ""
"**Saturation (Michaelis-Menten)**: Returns diminish as exposure "
"increases. The first $1,000$ impressions might drive $100$ conversions, "
"but the next $1,000$ might only drive $50$. Parameters $\\lambda$ and "
"$\\alpha$ control the shape of this curve."
msgstr ""
"**Saturación (Michaelis-Menten)**: los rendimientos disminuyen a medida que "
"aumenta la exposición. Las primeras $1,000$ impresiones podrían generar "
"$100$ conversiones, pero las siguientes $1,000$ podrían generar solo $50$. "
"Los parámetros $\\lambda$ y $\\alpha$ controlan la forma de esta curva."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:210008
#: 5229b85f1c894b25b1bc17ebcf048423
msgid ""
"We model only X4 → Y here because, according to our DAG, X4 is the **sole"
" marketing mediator** between all upstream channels and the outcome. By "
"getting this relationship right first, we can later propagate upstream "
"effects through it."
msgstr ""
"Aquí modelamos solo X4 → Y porque, según nuestro DAG, X4 es el **único "
"mediador de marketing** entre todos los canales anteriores y el resultado. "
"Al acertar primero con esta relación, más adelante podemos propagar a través"
" de ella los efectos de los canales anteriores."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:250002
#: 0b0f6c1989a24dbf8633d8fe99a78690
msgid "Indirect Model"
msgstr "Modelo indirecto"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:250004
#: 34d4b18938a64da5bcc079222e9c4def
msgid ""
"The second model captures how **upper-funnel activity (X1) influences "
"lower-funnel exposure (X4)**. This is the mediation link that allows us "
"to trace indirect effects."
msgstr ""
"El segundo modelo captura cómo la **actividad de la parte superior del "
"embudo (X1) influye en la exposición de la parte inferior del embudo (X4)**."
" Este es el vínculo de mediación que nos permite rastrear los efectos "
"indirectos."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:250006
#: 97ce90e62e1f47ebb560cfaa175515dd
msgid "**Why use differences?**"
msgstr "**¿Por qué usar diferencias?**"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:250008
#: 40363feed8d240e9a89a1730b1042026
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"If X1 and X4 are both trending or have unit roots (common in marketing "
"time series), a levels-on-levels regression $(X_{4,t} = \\alpha + \\beta "
"X_{1,t} + \\varepsilon_t)$ can produce spurious correlations. Taking "
"first differences removes trends and gives us a stationary relationship:"
msgstr ""
"Si X1 y X4 tienen tendencia o raíces unitarias (algo común en las series de "
"tiempo de marketing), una regresión de niveles sobre niveles $(X_{4,t} = "
"\\alpha + \\beta X_{1,t} + \\varepsilon_t)$ puede producir correlaciones "
"espurias. Tomar primeras diferencias elimina las tendencias y nos da una "
"relación estacionaria:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:250010
#: a5ae9124d5e64e7bb9304225df1239a5
#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\Delta X_{4,t} = \\beta \\cdot \\Delta X_{1,t} + \\varepsilon_t"
msgstr "\\Delta X_{4,t} = \\beta \\cdot \\Delta X_{1,t} + \\varepsilon_t"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:250012
#: 3b78a0b49b53449c98191dbc46195a2b
msgid "or equivalently:"
msgstr "o, de forma equivalente:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:250014
#: 0fa4d81d1269418489a822dfcea6573a
#, python-brace-format
msgid "X_{4,t} - X_{4,t-1} = \\beta \\cdot (X_{1,t} - X_{1,t-1})"
msgstr "X_{4,t} - X_{4,t-1} = \\beta \\cdot (X_{1,t} - X_{1,t-1})"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:250016
#: 8b23183cb4d44d159b40580782b20155
msgid ""
"This estimates the **instantaneous propagation**: when X1 increases by 1 "
"unit, how much does X4 change?"
msgstr ""
"Esto estima la **propagación instantánea**: cuando X1 aumenta en 1 unidad, "
"¿cuánto cambia X4?"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:250018
#: 24a23b858f2d494cbc261b307bf0a2c8
msgid ""
"**No adstock or saturation here.** We're assuming the X1 → X4 link is "
"approximately linear and immediate. All the nonlinear dynamics "
"(saturation, carryover) happen in the X4 → Y step, which we already "
"modeled above. This simplification keeps the mediation model "
"interpretable."
msgstr ""
"**Aquí no hay adstock ni saturación.** Suponemos que el vínculo X1 → X4 es "
"aproximadamente lineal e inmediato. Toda la dinámica no lineal (saturación, "
"efecto de arrastre) ocurre en el paso X4 → Y, que ya modelamos arriba. Esta "
"simplificación mantiene interpretable el modelo de mediación."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:270002
#: 67b0965bc5ca40ac8fae7143cf4aff18
msgid "Let's fit the mediation model:"
msgstr "Ajustemos el modelo de mediación:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:290002
#: 8849251d08a44aeaba9fd4f528921006
msgid ""
"For the sake of comparison, let's plot the posterior distribution of the "
"saturation parameter:"
msgstr ""
"Para comparar, grafiquemos la distribución posterior del parámetro de "
"saturación:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:310002
#: 43b119c4f74141a1b1c3b23970a66b5e
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"As shown in the advanced notebook "
"({ref}`mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach`), where we study the data "
"generating process, the saturation parameter is correctly recovered."
msgstr ""
"Como se muestra en el cuaderno avanzado "
"({ref}`mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach`), donde estudiamos el proceso "
"generador de datos, el parámetro de saturación se recupera correctamente."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:320002
#: 2ec1752a83144766a3845b95cf3f4130
msgid ""
"Let's now look into the contribution of the upper funnel channel to the "
"lower funnel channel."
msgstr ""
"Veamos ahora la contribución del canal de la parte superior del embudo al "
"canal de la parte inferior del embudo."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:340002
#: ca3e56c4509748b1b7c54e98af2c485b
msgid ""
"Again, from the data generating process, this contribution is correctly "
"estimated."
msgstr ""
"De nuevo, a partir del proceso generador de datos, esta contribución se "
"estima correctamente."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:350002
#: 4ef644db757b41dc9ad3443124f8f0b2
msgid ""
"Finally, we can visualize the posterior predictive mean of the lower "
"funnel channel."
msgstr ""
"Por último, podemos visualizar la media predictiva posterior del canal de la"
" parte inferior del embudo."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:370002
#: be4adfa2d20849b987782fc3dbffcb6c
msgid ""
"This baseline model is not fantastic, but it captures the general trend "
"of the data."
msgstr ""
"Este modelo base no es fantástico, pero captura la tendencia general de los "
"datos."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:380002
#: 01ef410fa4344fcd936e1ecd00091c89
msgid ""
"Now that we have both fitted models, we can use them to make "
"counterfactual predictions."
msgstr ""
"Ahora que tenemos ambos modelos ajustados, podemos usarlos para hacer "
"predicciones contrafactuales."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:390002
#: 69ab76e9880849848ba28943ac0a6727
msgid "Counterfactual Predictions"
msgstr "Predicciones contrafactuales"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:390004
#: cc9eaeec4e544cca9d3b8f943745502c
msgid ""
"Now comes the key question: **What would have happened if we had set X1 "
"to zero?** This is a **counterfactual prediction** — we use our models to"
" simulate an intervention we didn't actually observe."
msgstr ""
"Ahora llega la pregunta clave: **¿qué habría pasado si hubiéramos fijado X1 "
"en cero?** Esta es una **predicción contrafactual** — usamos nuestros "
"modelos para simular una intervención que no observamos realmente."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:390006
#: 510bca477e394c1e9b4f509b40d4af33
msgid "The causal effect of X1 on Y flows through this path:"
msgstr "El efecto causal de X1 sobre Y fluye a través de esta ruta:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:390008
#: fc40271d2e8f4d7f9e37b41d5cd85ed4
msgid "X_1 \\to X_4 \\to Y"
msgstr "X_1 \\to X_4 \\to Y"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:390010
#: 74b6669873974101bd791510e1cbd004
msgid "**Step-by-step counterfactual generation:**"
msgstr "**Generación contrafactual paso a paso:**"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:390012
#: 2bf50d7a984b4a4e80521a8a35990a07
msgid ""
"**Intervene on X1**: Set `impressions_x1 = 0` and compute "
"`impressions_x1_diff`"
msgstr ""
"**Intervenir sobre X1**: fije `impressions_x1 = 0` y calcule "
"`impressions_x1_diff`"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:390013
#: dea63738dc08448d816bc672610f1def
msgid ""
"**Predict counterfactual X4**: Use the mediation model to predict what X4"
" would have been without X1"
msgstr ""
"**Predecir el X4 contrafactual**: use el modelo de mediación para predecir "
"cuál habría sido X4 sin X1"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:390014
#: cb8261385f864dd08e334c71074e2021
msgid ""
"**Predict counterfactual Y**: Use the outcome model with the "
"counterfactual X4 as input"
msgstr ""
"**Predecir el Y contrafactual**: use el modelo del resultado con el X4 "
"contrafactual como entrada"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:390015
#: c88c61f766e64d1b86d0539e92bfc5f3
msgid ""
"**Calculate effect**: Compare predictions under $do(X_1=1)$ vs. "
"$do(X_1=0)$"
msgstr ""
"**Calcular el efecto**: compare las predicciones bajo $do(X_1=1)$ frente a "
"$do(X_1=0)$"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:390017
#: 2478b72028ce4848b84a6d870d7e7983
msgid ""
"This approach is called **g-computation** or **mediation formula** in "
"causal inference. We're propagating the intervention through each step of"
" the causal chain, respecting the dynamic transformations (adstock, "
"saturation) at each stage."
msgstr ""
"Este enfoque se denomina **g-computation** o **fórmula de mediación** en "
"inferencia causal. Estamos propagando la intervención a través de cada paso "
"de la cadena causal, respetando las transformaciones dinámicas (adstock, "
"saturación) en cada etapa."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:390020
#: cfb3da391c994fd1a3b122e3d55bca74
msgid ""
"**Why does this work?** By modeling each link separately (X1→X4 and "
"X4→Y), we can \"block\" X1's influence on X4, recompute X4, and see how "
"that change ripples through to Y. The difference between the factual and "
"counterfactual predictions is the **total causal effect** of X1 on Y."
msgstr ""
"**¿Por qué funciona esto?** Al modelar cada vínculo por separado (X1→X4 y "
"X4→Y), podemos \"bloquear\" la influencia de X1 sobre X4, recalcular X4 y "
"ver cómo ese cambio se propaga hasta Y. La diferencia entre las predicciones"
" factuales y contrafactuales es el **efecto causal total** de X1 sobre Y."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:400002
#: 600ba583b48d4947bec5f8bd3de8e06c
msgid "Let's start setting `impressions_x1` to zero:"
msgstr "Comencemos fijando `impressions_x1` en cero:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:420002
#: 84321a7861204b6b82ccde6bf35d1771
msgid ""
"Next, we used the fitted posterior to generate the counterfactual "
"predictions:"
msgstr ""
"A continuación, usamos la posterior ajustada para generar las predicciones "
"contrafactuales:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:440002
#: b4d59725877d4823815b77ee13d4fae0
msgid ""
"We can now plot the posterior predictive mean of the lower funnel channel"
" with the counterfactual predictions and compare them with the original "
"predictions."
msgstr ""
"Ahora podemos graficar la media predictiva posterior del canal de la parte "
"inferior del embudo con las predicciones contrafactuales y compararlas con "
"las predicciones originales."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:460002
#: 99b16943810c4496ad61d83c0868fb90
msgid ""
"As expected, on average most of the predicted impressions under the "
"counterfactual are lower than the original predictions."
msgstr ""
"Como era de esperar, en promedio la mayoría de las impresiones predichas "
"bajo el contrafactual son menores que las predicciones originales."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:470002
#: 5027d5041df84797801659c19fec73ee
msgid ""
"We now use these predictions to make counterfactual predictions for the "
"outcome."
msgstr ""
"Ahora usamos estas predicciones para hacer predicciones contrafactuales del "
"resultado."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:490002
#: 090d3d4e02ca4c9eb197d1e4e9abc2ee
msgid "Let's visualize the results:"
msgstr "Visualicemos los resultados:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:510002
#: e0909cf446a044b3a326f84313d65e64
msgid ""
"Finally, we can calculate the difference between the original and "
"counterfactual predictions and visualize the results:"
msgstr ""
"Por último, podemos calcular la diferencia entre las predicciones originales"
" y las contrafactuales y visualizar los resultados:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:540002
#: a7ef4c16e6264b728f4a6bade2ddf417
msgid "Conclusion"
msgstr "Conclusión"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:540004
#: ee5026aed81f4c238038ff9156324e8b
msgid ""
"In this notebook, we demonstrated how to measure **indirect upper-funnel "
"effects** using a mediation modeling approach. The key insights are:"
msgstr ""
"En este cuaderno, mostramos cómo medir los **efectos indirectos de la parte "
"superior del embudo** mediante un enfoque de modelado de mediación. Las "
"ideas clave son:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:540006
#: 0342d0f31cae40b2a771995d1fd08693
msgid ""
"**Respect causal structure**: Upper-funnel channels often don't directly "
"affect outcomes. Their influence flows through intermediate channels "
"(mediators)."
msgstr ""
"**Respetar la estructura causal**: los canales de la parte superior del "
"embudo a menudo no afectan directamente a los resultados. Su influencia "
"fluye a través de canales intermedios (mediadores)."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:540008
#: e17fb2d8ee0b42d8b9956ebb1241ccb3
msgid ""
"**Two-model approach**: By separating the mediation model (X1→X4) from "
"the outcome model (X4→Y), we can correctly attribute effects without "
"confounding."
msgstr ""
"**Enfoque de dos modelos**: al separar el modelo de mediación (X1→X4) del "
"modelo del resultado (X4→Y), podemos atribuir correctamente los efectos sin "
"confusión."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:540010
#: ebe9002be6b448609ed96378c2808759
msgid ""
"**Counterfactual reasoning**: To answer \"what would happen if we changed"
" X1?\", we propagate the intervention through each link of the causal "
"chain: $X_1 \\to X_4 \\to Y$."
msgstr ""
"**Razonamiento contrafactual**: para responder \"¿qué pasaría si cambiáramos"
" X1?\", propagamos la intervención a través de cada vínculo de la cadena "
"causal: $X_1 \\to X_4 \\to Y$."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:540012
#: 6d5bed60c56449d595cc892fce7a00ae
msgid ""
"**Dynamic effects matter**: The outcome model includes adstock and "
"saturation because marketing effects carry over time and show diminishing"
" returns."
msgstr ""
"**Los efectos dinámicos importan**: el modelo del resultado incluye adstock "
"y saturación porque los efectos del marketing se arrastran en el tiempo y "
"muestran rendimientos decrecientes."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:540014
#: b4d68f2088044cb097420913b5fbfa3e
msgid ""
"**Key takeaway:** Standard MMMs that throw all channels into one model "
"will misattribute upper-funnel contributions. A causal approach that "
"models the funnel structure explicitly gives more accurate and defensible"
" effect estimates."
msgstr ""
"**Idea clave:** los MMM estándar que meten todos los canales en un solo "
"modelo atribuirán mal las contribuciones de la parte superior del embudo. Un"
" enfoque causal que modela explícitamente la estructura del embudo ofrece "
"estimaciones de efectos más precisas y defendibles."

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:540016
#: f8f2ba911c7c4a628902afeaaabebbb6
msgid "For a comprehensive treatment including:"
msgstr "Para un tratamiento exhaustivo que incluye:"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:540017
#: 4af29f74a95a42e2b6388ca196cc6189
msgid "Detailed data generation process"
msgstr "Proceso detallado de generación de datos"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:540018
#: 2568c9de34db4f33a368f71495a8928a
msgid "Theoretical foundations (backdoor criterion, structural causal models)"
msgstr ""
"Fundamentos teóricos (criterio de puerta trasera, modelos causales "
"estructurales)"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:540019
#: a4778e41a5de41e1ae5bc4ca6cd2f6a4
msgid "Comparison with naive \"all-in\" models"
msgstr "Comparación con modelos \"todo incluido\" ingenuos"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:540020
#: 5997d3b89afc4ce1916b1837963d67a2
msgid "Out-of-sample validation"
msgstr "Validación fuera de muestra"

#: ../source/notebooks/mmm/mmm_intro_upper_funnel.ipynb:540022
#: e1dd13072f4e44c484d0e4279fb22dbc
#, python-brace-format
msgid "see the advanced version: {ref}`mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach`."
msgstr ""
"consulte la versión avanzada: {ref}`mmm_upper_funnel_causal_approach`."

